### MigraPilot Brain — service environment  (TEMPLATE)
#
# Installed at «BRAIN_ENV_FILE», owned root:«BRAIN_SERVICE_GROUP», mode 0640.
# Never world-readable: this file may carry provider and gateway secrets.
#
# Every variable below was read from apps/brain-service source. Nothing invented.

# ── bind: PRIVATE INTERFACE ONLY ───────────────────────────────────────────
# src/config/env.ts:57 — defaults to 127.0.0.1 when unset.
#
# 127.0.0.1  → Brain reachable only from the same host. Correct if the consumer
#              Next.js server runs on this host.
# «PRIVATE_IP» → the internal-network address, required only if the consumer runs
#              on a DIFFERENT host. Verify the interface exists first.
#
# NEVER 0.0.0.0. Binding all interfaces is what makes a private service public.
MIGRAPILOT_BRAIN_HOST=127.0.0.1
MIGRAPILOT_BRAIN_PORT=3988

# ── persistent state ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# ⛔ BLOCKER — DO NOT DEPLOY TO PRODUCTION IN THE CURRENT STATE.
#
# MigraPilot's production persistence architecture is PostgreSQL (Prisma),
# following MigraTeck database standards for ownership, backup and restore.
#
# brain-service does NOT implement that today. Verified in source:
#   • src/engine/persistence/ contains only sqliteStore.ts
#   • src/server.ts:62 imports SqliteDurableStore directly
#   • no adapter-selection env var exists — SQLite is hardcoded
#   • package.json has no prisma / @prisma/client / pg dependency
#   • src/engine/persistence/types.ts:6 describes a "Postgres+pgvector adapter"
#     as something that "can back a hosted/multi-tenant deployment LATER"
#
# So there is nothing to point at a database yet. Implementing the PostgreSQL
# adapter against the existing store interface is a prerequisite DEVELOPMENT
# task, not a deployment setting.
#
# MIGRAPILOT_STATE_DB is deliberately left UNSET. Setting it would configure a
# VM-local SQLite database as production state — outside the ecosystem's
# database standards and its backup/restore path. Acceptance check 11 fails
# closed if it is set, and fails closed while no PostgreSQL adapter exists.
#
# When the adapter lands, expect something of this shape (name to be confirmed
# by the implementation, not assumed here):
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:5432/DBNAME?schema=public

NODE_ENV=production

# ── governed coding ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave disabled for the consumer gate. The consumer is observation-only and
# never starts runs; enabling this on a server with no developer workspace
# would configure a capability nothing can legitimately use.
MIGRAPILOT_CODING_ENABLED=false
# Only meaningful when the above is true. Absolute, canonical roots.
# MIGRAPILOT_CODING_WORKSPACE_ROOTS=

# ── application-to-Brain authentication (FORWARD-LOOKING) ──────────────────
# The Brain already implements a trusted-gateway pattern:
#   x-migrapilot-principal      asserted principal
#   x-migrapilot-gateway-secret shared secret, must match this value
# (src/engine/capability/operatorPrincipal.ts:77-101)
#
# IMPORTANT: today this is enforced ONLY on engineerRoutes.ts. It does NOT
# protect /api/ai/conversations tenancy, so setting it does not by itself
# secure the consumer path. It is the natural in-house precedent for extending
# identity-aware auth to /api/ai/* as defence in depth — a Brain change, not a
# deployment setting.
# MIGRAPILOT_GATEWAY_SECRET=

# ── model providers ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Populate per the environment's provider policy. Left blank here deliberately:
# provider credentials are out of scope for the infrastructure gate.
# MIGRAPILOT_LOCAL_PROVIDER=
# MIGRAPILOT_PROVIDER_URL=
